<!--
  DROID_DISTRESS_CALL_REPOINT_1 (C7). Ruling 13
  (DROID_UNIFIED_FRAMEWORK_DESIGN.md §0): "Distress Call quest: re-point to DW
  kinds - it becomes the wild/crashed-droid rescue."

  Target: btd.gbp.shippack.kotor.vge's IncidentDef BTD_DroidDistressCall
  (workshop 3614012898, also duplicated byte-identical inside its dependency
  btd.remix.gravshipblueprints, workshop 3575162262 - both copies live under a
  path named 1.6/Mods/BTD_KotOR_Droids/ and both are LoadFolders-gated:
  <li IfModActiveAll="guy762.KotORDroids,btd.gbp.shippack.kotor.vge">
  (REMIX's own LoadFolders.xml) / <li IfModActive="guy762.KotORDroids">
  (the VGE shippack's own LoadFolders.xml). CONFIRMED the open question in
  DROID_PROGRAM_STATE_2026-09-06.md: yes, gated on guy762.KotORDroids being
  active - the quest content does not exist at all without it. Guarded with
  PatchOperationConditional testing the target node itself (rimworld-modding's
  own guidance: MayRequire/FindMod check the MOD, Conditional checks the DEF -
  the def's existence here is a LoadFolders fact, not just an installed-mod
  fact, so Conditional is the guard that actually matches reality). Once
  guy762.KotORDroids is retired
  (D2), this whole folder stops loading and the patch below simply matches
  nothing from then on (harmless no-op, per this repo's own "patch matches
  nothing logs nothing" doctrine) - the permanent, donor-independent
  wild/crashed-droid rescue is DROIDWORKS_WILD_DROIDS_1 (E4), explicitly out
  of scope here.

  CORRECTION to the design doc's "5 KotORDroidColonist_* refs": live-read off
  disk, the modExtension's rewardDroidKindDefs list actually names 19 (not
  5) KotORDroidColonist_* kinds. All 19 confirmed as real PawnKindDefs in
  guy762.KotORDroids's PawnKinds_PlayerDroids.xml, and all 19 have a 1:1
  Droidworks absorption in src/RimStarWars/Droidworks/Defs/PawnKinds_KotOR.xml
  (RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_<suffix>, same suffix, same race-per-kind
  mapping) - repointed below.

  Reframe (player-facing text): questNameRules/questDescriptionRules and the
  IncidentDef's letterLabel/letterText were already donor-neutral ("distress
  call from a crashed freighter", "the other droids ... have gone haywire and
  become hostile") - no literal "KotOR" string anywhere in the quest's or
  incident's player-facing text, so no text patch is needed for the reframe;
  the kind repoint alone completes it (the reward pawn's own PawnKindDef
  labels are already generic - "war droid", "protocol droid", etc., never
  "KotOR" anything).

  Explicitly NOT touched (out of scope for this item):
  - IncidentDef's hostileFactionDef guy762_KotORFaction_RogueDroids (the site's
    hostile spawn faction, hidden, label "rogue droid collective"). Ruling 2
    bans a rogue droid faction going forward and D2's own supersession note
    already retires this concept with kotordroids; repointing it is a
    mechanism change (which faction fields the site's hostiles) that belongs
    to whoever executes D2/E4, not this narrow kind+text repoint.
  - eligibleShipLabels, SitePartDef, QuestScriptDef node tree: none of these
    name a KotOR-specific kind or donor string.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/IncidentDef[defName="BTD_DroidDistressCall"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="RWM_BTD_Remix_GravshipBlueprints.BTD_ModExtension_DroidDistressCallSettings"]/rewardDroidKindDefs</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/IncidentDef[defName="BTD_DroidDistressCall"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="RWM_BTD_Remix_GravshipBlueprints.BTD_ModExtension_DroidDistressCallSettings"]/rewardDroidKindDefs</xpath>
      <value>
        <rewardDroidKindDefs>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_T3UD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_3CUD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ITUD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_R8009UD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3LD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GE3PD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KX12UPD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KX12APD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_MPDMkI</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KM1MD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_KM1HMD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_SentWD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_DevWD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_DevAD</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ADMkI</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ADMkI_sf</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ADMkIV</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_ADMkIV_sith</li>
          <li>RSW_DW_KotORDroidColonist_GOTO</li>
        </rewardDroidKindDefs>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
